    },
    {
      "text": "requirement from the full n-dimensional state space to a",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        256.7580261230469,
        558.0009155273438,
        265.60479736328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "structure parameterized by energy and the ergodic index α.",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        268.7130432128906,
        558.0009765625,
        277.559814453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In particular, reachability can be achieved by covering a set",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        280.9170837402344,
        558.0009765625,
        289.5048522949219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "whose effective dimension is that of α plus one, accounting",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        292.6230163574219,
        558.0010375976562,
        301.46978759765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for energy, without requiring demonstrations throughout the",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        304.8270568847656,
        558.0009765625,
        313.4148254394531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "state space.",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        316.7830505371094,
        360.5323486328125,
        325.3708190917969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "B. Existence of the Chain Policy",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        336.82305908203125,
        447.8246154785156,
        345.41082763671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Theorem 2 provides conditions on the assignment set K",
      "bbox": [
        323.1630554199219,
        351.6690979003906,
        557.851806640625,
        361.29296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "under which the chain policy guarantees target reachability.",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        364.3414001464844,
        558.0010375976562,
        373.2479553222656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "However, it is not a priori clear whether such conditions can",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        376.29638671875,
        558.0009765625,
        385.20294189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "be satisfied using a finite set of control segments. To address",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        388.2513732910156,
        558.0010375976562,
        397.1579284667969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this question, we first derive upper and lower bounds on the",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        400.2073669433594,
        558.0009155273438,
        409.1139221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "quantities that govern energy decrease and recurrence, which",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        412.162353515625,
        558.0009765625,
        421.06890869140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "will allow us to establish existence and sample complexity",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        424.1173400878906,
        558.0010986328125,
        433.0238952636719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "guarantees for K.",
      "bbox": [
        313.2000427246094,
        435.3550109863281,
        384.6119079589844,
        444.9788818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lemma 1 (Velocity and Hitting-Time Bounds). Under As-",
